===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|Sikhim||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|en|sip|སུ་ཁྱིམ}}; The most widely accepted theory is that it is a combination of two Limbu words: su, which means "new", and khyim, which means "palace" or "house". The name is believed to be a reference to the palace built by the state's first ruler, Phuntsog Namgyal.

